note OM-1 TWIN of inline-order.om (inline removed, om2 line made a note) for the pinned compiler
note 734f0a39: same expectations, so OM-1 semantics cross-check the oracle now.
note Contract section 4 lines 93-98 (inline) and 102-104 (folding): arguments are evaluated left to
note right before the body, exactly as for a call; traps, their order and codes are unchanged; removing
note inline changes nothing (twin inline-order-plain.om). One stdin byte selects a case:
note   A f (mk 10 1) (mk 3 2): markers 1 then 2, then 11/3 = 3        exit 0
note   B f (div 1 0) (add 2147483647 1): first argument traps 2      exit 102
note   C f (add 2147483647 1) (div 1 0): first argument traps 1      exit 101
note   D f 2147483647 0: body add traps 1 before body div traps 2   exit 101 (constant args: no fold)
note   E f 5 0: body div by 0 traps 2                               exit 102 (constant args: no fold)
note   F f (mk 1 1) (div 1 0): marker 1 printed, then trap 2         exit 102
note   G f (div 1 0) (mk 1 2): trap 2 before the marker              exit 102
note   H g -5, g 7: early ret inside an inlined body: 0 then 14      exit 0
note   I g (mk 7 3): an argument used twice in the body is evaluated once: marker 3, then 14
note Expected stdout: oracle/s3s4/exp/inline-order-*.out (python3, oracle/s3s4/oracle.py).
note OM-1 unit: this line replaces the om2 line
fn f a int b int to int
x = add a 1
ret div x b
end
fn g a int to int
if lt a 0
ret 0
end
ret mul a 2
end
fn mk v int t ulong to int
pu t
ret v
end
fn main to int
s = new uchar 1 0
r = read 0 s 0 1
k = get s 0
if eq k 65
pu ulong f mk 10 1 mk 3 2
end
if eq k 66
pu ulong f div int 1 0 add int 2147483647 1
end
if eq k 67
pu ulong f add int 2147483647 1 div int 1 0
end
if eq k 68
pu ulong f 2147483647 0
end
if eq k 69
pu ulong f 5 0
end
if eq k 70
pu ulong f mk 1 1 div int 1 0
end
if eq k 71
pu ulong f div int 1 0 mk 1 2
end
if eq k 72
pu ulong g -5
pu ulong g 7
end
if eq k 73
pu ulong g mk 7 3
end
ret 0
end
